<article id="post-851" class="post-851 page type-page status-publish hentry">
	<header class="entry-header">
		<div class="pageWidth">
			<h1 class="entry-title">

			Accelerator			</h1>
						  <ul>
			  <li class="page_item page-item-879"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130622072314/http://velocityindiana.org/accelerator/current-teams/">Current Teams</a></li>
<li class="page_item page-item-9"><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130622072314/http://velocityindiana.org/accelerator/mentors/">Mentors</a></li>
			  </ul>
					</div>
	</header><!-- .entry-header -->

	<div class="entry-content pageWidth">
		<p class="leadText">Our flagship program is our business accelerator. We provide direct funding &amp; mentoring for promising young companies through the critical early stages.</p>
<p><!--<a href="http://faq" class="readMore">Learn more by reading our FAQ</a>&#8211;></p>
			</div><!-- .entry-content -->
</article>

				
						<div class="pageWidth">				
	        	<article id="acceleratorFunding" class="offering tabContainer is-open" style="display: block;">
					<div id="fundingSpot" class="spot largeOneThird">
						<img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20130622072314im_/http://velocityindiana.org/wp-content/themes/velocity/img/spot-funding.png"/>
					</div>
					<div class="largeTwoThird">
						<h3>Funding</h3>
<p>In addition to business support services, each team will receive:</p>
<ul>
<li>$20,000 in exchange for a small amount of equity in the company</li>
<li>We provide approximately $450,000 worth of perks, including major discounts and upgrades on core services from program sponsors.</li>
<li>For companies that enter the accelerator and make sufficient progress during the program, Velocity Ventures, a side-car fund, may invest up to $100k toward the company&#8217;s seed round of funding on the same terms as other investors.</li>
</ul>
					</div>
				</article>
	        	<article id="acceleratorMentorship" class="offering largeOneHalf tabContainer">
					<div id="mentorshipSpot" class="spot">
						<img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20130622072314im_/http://velocityindiana.org/wp-content/themes/velocity/img/spot-mentorship.png"/>
					</div>
					<div class="">
						<h3>Mentorship</h3>
<p>In addition to our funding &amp; workspace, you&#8217;ll have access to some of the most talented, driven, innovative and interesting people in the area.</p>
<p><a class="button_b" href="/web/20130622072314/http://velocityindiana.org/about/mentors">Our mentors</a></p>
					</div>
				</article>
	        	<article id="acceleratorWorkspace" class="offering largeOneHalf tabContainer">
					<div id="workspaceSpot" class="spot">
						<img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20130622072314im_/http://velocityindiana.org/wp-content/themes/velocity/img/spot-workspace.png"/>
					</div>
					<div class="">
						<h3>Workspace</h3>
<p>Our membership boasts a lively camaraderie of social and interactive workers who break free from the isolation of working from home and instead get going.</p>
<p><a class="button_b" href="/web/20130622072314/http://velocityindiana.org/about/workspace">Plans &amp; pricing</a></p>
					</div>
				</article>
				<article id="acceleratorProgram" class="offering clear tabContainer">
					<div id="programSpot" class="spot">
						<img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20130622072314im_/http://velocityindiana.org/wp-content/themes/velocity/img/spot-program.png"/>
					</div>
					<div class="programDetails">
						<p class="leadText">The team’s at Velocity will take part in a program based on the Lean LaunchPad approach to building startup companies.</p>
						<div class="largeOneThird">
							<h3>Crafting a Hypothesis</h3>
							<p>Teams will apply the scientific method to there business model by breaking it down into an individual hypothesis</p>
						</div>
						<div class="largeOneThird">
							<h3>Test &amp; Experiment</h3>
							<p>Teams will build a simple and inexpensive experiment. Then we <em>get out of the building,</em> talking to customers &amp; partners to test &amp; validate our assumptions.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="largeOneThird">
							<h3>Response &amp; Iteration</h3>
							<p>If (&amp; when) the hypothesis fails, we pivot the business model and repeat the process until the entire model is proven; no longer based on extensive assumptions.</p>
						</div>
						<p>The Lean LaunchPad was popularized by Steve Blank and is taught at Standford, UC Berkley and other Universities across the US. It has been applied to accelerator programs, the NSF, intrapeneurship programs, as well as high school and middle schools students. The approach enables a startup to build and validate that they have a viable business model before they attempt to build and scale a company. This is done using Alexander Osterwalder’s Business Model Canvas as the means to document the model. It further employs Blank’s Customer Development approach to translate business model assumptions into facts by running experiments.</p>
						<p>This approach is not a one size fits all approach. It is applied in a different and unique way to each company, depending on their industry, level of development and experience. It is also not a prescriptive methodology, but rather a general approach that applies the principles learned over the past two decades on how to build successful, scalable companies.</p>
					</div>
				</article>
